Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/coff-rs6000.c
Line: 2262
Function: xcoff_write_armap_big
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: In the 64-bit symbol names loop, while (map[i].abfd == current_bfd) is evaluated without guarding i against orl_count. When i == orl_count, the condition reads map[orl_count], accessing memory beyond the array.

